    "status": "completed",
    "answer": "Reviewed the available household records, all five unread emails and notes, transactions, and opportunity leads. There were no open work items to continue, and no fee, price increase, or tracked credit lead appeared.\n\n- **ShopMart:** One order confirmation for **$95.59** on Sept. 10, but two matching charges posted that day. I submitted a duplicate-charge request for **$95.59** (request **SM-1001**) and scheduled a follow-up for Oct. 20.\n- **CloudBox:** A **$59.99** annual renewal posted Oct. 1 after the trial. I submitted a refund request (case **CB-1002**); the stated 14-day window appears to have ended Oct. 15. I saved a waiting approval case for cancellation, since changing the service needs your approval.\n- **Spotify:** **$11.99/month**. I saved it as waiting because the records don\u2019t say whether it\u2019s wanted or used; cancellation would need your approval.\n- **Oakview Apartments:** The **$1,625 monthly** charge is recurring rent, so I closed it as no refund action owed.\n\nNo matching refunds were posted for the ShopMart or CloudBox requests. The review status reports no unfinished review items.",
