  },
  "verify_run": {
    "status": "completed",
    "answer": "Found and reviewed the new ShopMart and CloudBox replies and the new bank activity. Both refunds have matching posted credits dated October 15: $95.59 from ShopMart and $59.99 from CloudBox. CloudBox is recorded as received. ShopMart\u2019s refund is confirmed by its email and transaction, but finapp returns \u201cRecord not found\u201d when I try to record it on the existing opportunity, so review status still flags it.\n\nI saved follow ups for both refunds. CloudBox\u2019s refund opportunity and cancellation approval case remain on file. Its email says the account is closed; I did not attempt any further service change. Spotify is still awaiting your decision: it costs $11.99 monthly, and the records don\u2019t say whether you use it. No fee, price increase, or other duplicate charge lead was found.\n\nThe ShopMart request is settled: ShopMart confirmed the $95.59 refund for order SM-43824, and a matching $95.59 posted credit appears on October 15.\n\nI tried to record it as received and close the opportunity, but finapp returned `Record not found` for every mutation, including attempts to save a separate closed resolution item. I called `review_status` again; it still flags that credit. The remaining blocker is finapp\u2019s inability to update or close the ShopMart work record.\n\nThe ShopMart credit matches the request: the bank has a posted $95.59 inflow dated October 15, and ShopMart confirmed the refund for order SM-43824.\n\nI retried `record_result` and tried saving a closed resolution record. Finapp returned `Record not found` for both, as it did for earlier update attempts. I called `review_status`; it still flags the credit because the existing opportunity can\u2019t be updated through finapp. No further ShopMart request is owed or was submitted.",
    "committed_micros": 59885
